      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "exigent circumstances doctrine allows offcers to enter a home without a warrant in certain situations, including: to fght a fre and investigate its cause; to prevent the imminent destruction of evidence; to engage in hot pursuit of a feeing felon or prevent a suspect's escape; to address a threat to the safety of law enforcement offcers or the general public; to render emergency assistance to an injured occupant; or to protect an occupant who is threatened with serious injury."
    }
